orname{sin}⁡(4\\pi )\\,k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1}\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16)\\,j+\\frac{5}{5}\\cdot 0\\,k \\\\  & =1\\,i+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16)\\,j+0\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-4,\\,\\sqrt{3t+7}⟩,$ calculate $r(5).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$r(5)=⟨$\n{{field-1}} $,$\n\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a52558c8-d1b8-5f58-a439-fc5376186768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575583 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute $t=5$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(5) & =⟨{5}^{2}-4,\\,\\sqrt{3\\cdot 5+7}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨21,\\,\\sqrt{22}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575595 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575595 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50357" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575595 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575595 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨2t-1,\\,\\sqrt{t+1}⟩,$ calculate $r(3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575595 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bab955aa-96ab-5495-ba71-684f1eacabcc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575595 #edb/ref 1074 "We  substitute $t=3$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨2(3)-1,\\,\\sqrt{3+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575455 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348662" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $g(t)=⟨{3}^{\\,t-1},\\,{log}_{3}⁡({t}^{2}+2t),\\,{sec}^{2}\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{4})-1⟩$ at $t=1?$\n\n$g(1)=⟨$\n{{field-1}} $,\\,$\n{{field-2}} $,\\,$\n{{field-3}} $⟩$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc70b07d-530b-5e77-9200-c7de006703f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575600 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t=1$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(1) & =⟨{3}^{1-1},\\,{log}_{3}⁡({1}^{2}+2(1)),\\,{sec}^{2}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{log}_{3}⁡(3),\\,{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348676" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-21,\\,\\sqrt{3t-9}⟩,$ calculate $r(6).$\n\n$r(6)=⟨$\n{{field-1}} $,$\n\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d0d01a34-dbf9-5949-a688-edf940f34604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575603 #edb/ref 1074 "We substitute $t=6$ into our function, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(6) & =⟨{6}^{2}-21,\\,\\sqrt{3\\cdot 6-9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨36-21,\\,\\sqrt{9}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨15,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-348682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575615 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}),\\,\\frac{4}{t-1}⟩,$ what is $|r(3)|?$\n\n$|r(3)|=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e8bf0613-dc2d-57fb-b4e9-45d51faad202" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575615 #edb/ref 1074 "Evaluating the function at $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}),\\,\\frac{4}{3-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(3)| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575618 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575618 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123288" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575618 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575618 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $|r(1)|$ given that $r(t)=⟨8{t}^{2}-5,\\,2t+2,\\,5t⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575618 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed1928c0-77ed-571b-8c4d-3959f2119041" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575618 #edb/ref 1074 "Evaluating the function at $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =⟨8({1}^{2})-5,\\,2(1)+2,\\,5(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,4,\\,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(1)| & =\\sqrt{{(3)}^{2}+{(4)}^{2}+(5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{50} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575620 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575620 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161508" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575620 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575620 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\end{bmatrix}$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575620 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f479be92-cf45-5de7-9956-484ec8fcce81" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575620 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575623 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575623 #edb/ref 1069 "q-160783" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575623 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575623 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of $f(s)=⟨{s}^{2},\\,3s-2,\\,-s⟩$ at $s=1?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575623 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa3121c1-bbfa-5933-8aaf-25e82847d915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575623 #edb/ref 1074 "To evaluate, we substitute $s=1$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =⟨{1}^{2},\\,3\\cdot 1-2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(s)$ at $s=1$ is the vector $⟨1,1,-1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
